42:["$","ol","ol-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"简化错误处理："}]," 如果同时存在多个 ",["$","code","code-0",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}],"，就会变得非常复杂去确定如何处理它们，尤其是在它们之间存在依赖关系的时候。一个 ",["$","code","code-1",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 应该表示一个不可恢复的错误，如果有多个这样的错误同时存在，程序的状态可能会变得非常不确定。"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"保持一致性："}]," ",["$","code","code-0",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 通常表示程序中出现了严重错误，可能会破坏程序的一致性或安全性。如果允许多个 ",["$","code","code-1",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 同时存在，就很难保证程序状态的一致性，因为不同的 ",["$","code","code-2",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 可能需要回退不同的操作。"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"避免资源泄漏："}]," ",["$","code","code-0",{"className":"$undefined","children":"defer"}]," 语句用于确保资源被释放，例如文件和锁。如果在处理一个 ",["$","code","code-1",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 的过程中，又发生了另一个 ",["$","code","code-2",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}],"，可能会导致 ",["$","code","code-3",{"className":"$undefined","children":"defer"}]," 语句中剩余的清理代码无法执行，从而引起资源泄漏。"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"控制流程清晰："}]," ",["$","code","code-0",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 和 ",["$","code","code-1",{"className":"$undefined","children":"recover"}]," 的设计使得错误的控制流程清晰且可预测。一旦一个 ",["$","code","code-2",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 被 ",["$","code","code-3",{"className":"$undefined","children":"recover"}]," 捕获，程序可以选择是否继续执行，或者是通过重新 ",["$","code","code-4",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 来终止程序。这种决策过程在多个 ",["$","code","code-5",{"className":"$undefined","children":"panic"}]," 情况下会变得复杂且难以管理。"]}],"\n"]}]
